    {
      "id": "REQ-9641",
      "position_title": "Executive / Senior Executive – Analytical Research & Development (Review)",
      "position_code": "",
      "department": "Analytical Development",
      "business_unit": "",
      "location": "IITM ,Taramani",
      "position_type": "New Position",
      "budgeted_ctc": "240000",
      "grade": "",
      "employment_type": "Full-Time",
      "number_of_openings": "1",
      "required_experience": "",
      "qualification": "",
      "key_skills": "",
      "job_description": "Executive / Senior Executive – Analytical Research & Development (Review)\r\n\r\nCompany: Axxelent Pharma Science Private Limited\r\nDepartment: Analytical Research & Development (ARD) – Review\r\nLocation: R&D Unit, IIT Madras Research Park, Taramani, Chennai\r\nDesignation: Executive / Senior Executive\r\nEmployment Type: Full-Time\r\n\r\nAbout the Role\r\n\r\nAxxelent Pharma Science Pvt. Ltd. is seeking an experienced and detail-oriented Executive / Senior Executive – Analytical Research & Development (Review) to join our Analytical R&D team. The role is responsible for reviewing analytical documents, ensuring data integrity, regulatory compliance, and supporting the development team by providing technical review and guidance throughout the product development lifecycle.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities\r\nReview analytical methods, protocols, reports, raw data, and technical documentation for accuracy, completeness, and compliance.\r\nVerify analytical calculations, chromatograms, spectra, and laboratory records.\r\nEvaluate experimental results, trends, out-of-specification (OOS), out-of-trend (OOT), and deviations.\r\nEnsure compliance with ALCOA+ principles and Data Integrity requirements.\r\nReview analytical method validation, method transfer, verification, stability, and routine analytical reports.\r\nEnsure compliance with cGMP, GLP, ICH, USFDA, EU GMP, MHRA, WHO, and other applicable regulatory guidelines.\r\nIdentify documentation gaps and provide constructive feedback to analytical scientists.\r\nSupport investigations related to laboratory deviations, OOS, OOT, CAPA, and change controls.\r\nEnsure proper documentation, traceability, and archival of analytical records.\r\nCollaborate with Formulation Development, Quality Assurance, Regulatory Affairs, and other cross-functional teams.\r\nParticipate in internal and external audits by providing analytical documentation and technical support.\r\nContribute to continuous improvement initiatives to enhance laboratory documentation and review processes.\r\nRequired Qualifications\r\nM.Pharm (Pharmaceutical Analysis / Quality Assurance / Pharmaceutics)\r\nB.Pharm\r\nM.Sc. Chemistry / Analytical Chemistry / Organic Chemistry\r\nExperience\r\n4–7 years of relevant experience in:\r\nAnalytical Research & Development\r\nAnalytical Review\r\nQuality Control Review\r\nPharmaceutical R&D Documentation Review\r\nRequired Technical Skills\r\nHPLC, UPLC, GC, UV, FTIR, Dissolution, KF, TOC, ICP-MS (preferred)\r\nAnalytical Method Development & Validation\r\nMethod Transfer & Verification\r\nStability Studies\r\nDocumentation Review\r\nData Integrity (ALCOA+)\r\ncGMP / GLP Documentation\r\nOOS / OOT Investigation\r\nChange Control & CAPA\r\nTechnical Report Review\r\nICH Guidelines (Q2, Q3, Q6, Q8, Q9, Q10)\r\nUSFDA, MHRA, WHO, EU GMP regulatory expectations\r\nDesired Competencies\r\nStrong analytical and critical thinking skills.\r\nExcellent attention to detail.\r\nEffective documentation review and interpretation.\r\nGood communication and interpersonal skills.\r\nAbility to work independently and within cross-functional teams.\r\nProblem-solving mindset with a focus on quality and compliance.\r\nTime management and prioritization skills.\r\nPreferred Experience\r\n\r\nCandidates with prior experience in any of the following will have an added advantage:\r\n\r\nInjectable dosage forms\r\nOral solid dosage forms\r\nSemi-solid formulations\r\nRegulatory audit exposure\r\nContract Development & Manufacturing Organization (CDMO)\r\nAnalytical review for global regulatory submissions\r\nWhy Join Axxelent Pharma Science?\r\nOpportunity to work on global pharmaceutical development projects.\r\nExposure to advanced analytical technologies and regulatory standards.\r\nCollaborative and innovation-driven work culture.\r\nCareer growth in a fast-growing CDMO environment.\r\nContinuous learning and professional development opportunities.\r\nWork Location\r\n\r\nAxxelent Pharma Science Pvt. Ltd.\r\nR&D Unit, IIT Madras Research Park\r\nKanagam Road, Taramani\r\nChennai – 600113\r\n\r\nApply Now\r\n\r\nInterested candidates may share their updated resume to:\r\n\r\nEmail: corpHR@axxelent.com / vrpradeep@axxelent.com\r\n\r\nWhatsApp: +91 95005 93997 / +91 97890 98123",
